course: dictionary
lesson: 5263
title: Words that bump and push
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To jostle means to push and bump against people, especially in a crowd. «Taffy asks for a little bit of stick or something between each word, so's they won't rub up against each other and jostle.» Words crammed together would bump into each other, so jostle here means bumping against one another.
explain: To find the meaning, read the words around jostle and ask what would fit. Rub up against and bump are clues. Try your meaning in the sentence: "so they won't bump against each other" still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: Jostle can also mean to compete hard for something. «Players jostling for a place in the team» are not pushing anyone; they are fighting to win a spot. The context tells you which meaning the writer means.
fact: Jostle is a verb: jostle, jostles, jostled, jostling. It can also be a noun: a jostle.
fact: «Jostle» means to push and bump against people, especially in a crowd.
fact: «Jostle» can also mean to compete hard for something, such as a place in a team.
fact: Crowds jostle at the school gate or on the bus, so take care on stairs.
fact: In «Alice in Wonderland», the animals crowd and jostle around Alice after the Pool of Tears.
exercise: «Taffy asks for a little space between words so they will not jostle.» What does jostle mean here? | To stand far apart | *To bump and push against each other | To sleep quietly | To sing loudly
exercise: Players are jostling for a place in the team. What does jostling mean? | To cheer loudly from the stands | *To compete hard for something | To leave the team | To push people off a bus
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you the animals push around Alice: | Tears | Alice | Pool | *jostle
test: «Crowds jostle on the stairs at home time.» What does jostle tell you about the stairs? | *People may push and bump each other | People are asleep on the steps | The stairs are empty and quiet | The stairs are brand new
test: Which form of jostle is a noun? | jostling | jostled | *a jostle | jostles
exam: Ella says jostle means to hug gently. Which clues in the sentence show she is wrong? | Ella is right, the word means gentle | Hugging is a kind of jostle | *The words crowds and bump show it means knocking against people | The word gently tells you the meaning
